# Grace period in seconds after each scheduled time, before the machine powers
# off (input for run_onchange_9_1_auto_poweroff_timer.sh). 0 = immediate.
#
# While waiting, a CANCELLABLE shutdown is scheduled (`shutdown -P +<min>`), so
# the pending power-off can be canceled with `sudo shutdown -c`. systemd's
# `+N` schedule is minute-granular, so 300s rounds to a 5-minute countdown.
300
